{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateFSTrichotomy"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.realType_induced_fails_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.realType_induced_fails_gate","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L137-L144","doc":"**The real-type instance, in one line.**  A real-type irrep occurring with\npositive multiplicity fails the gate outright — the `Sym²`-induced case, once\nits Frobenius–Schur label is read as `real`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.selfDual_candidate_not_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.selfDual_candidate_not_three","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L123-L135","doc":"**The route-E prune.**  A self-dual candidate is not the missing\nthree-dimensional flavour object.  Stated over the companion's model; the\n`hsd` hypothesis is the `FSType` reading of §2's self-duality and is\ndeliberately not derived from it (see the scope note). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.induced_is_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.induced_is_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L110-L119","doc":"**Every induced three-dimensional object is self-dual.**  Combining\n`SelfDualSource` with §2: whatever `V` the source supplies, `Sym² V` is\nself-dual — so the composite `π₁ → SL(2) → SL(3)` can never be complex type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.symSquare_selfDual_of_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.symSquare_selfDual_of_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L95-L108","doc":"**The structural step.**  If `V` is self-dual then so is `Sym² V`.\n\n`V* ≅ V` gives `Sym²(V*) ≅ Sym² V` by congruence, and `Sym²(V*) ≅ (Sym² V)*`\nby compatibility; transitivity closes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.symm","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L91-L91","doc":"`iso` is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.trans","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L89-L89","doc":"`iso` is transitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.congr","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L87-L87","doc":"`iso` is respected by `Sym²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.commutes","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L85-L85","doc":"`Sym²(V*) ≅ (Sym² V)*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SymSquareDualCompatible","kind":"structure","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L81-L91","doc":"`Sym²` commutes with dualisation up to isomorphism, and `iso` is a\ncongruence for it.  The two halves the next theorem needs, bundled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SelfDualSource","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.SelfDualSource","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L76-L79","doc":"Every representation of the source group is self-dual — the `SL(2)`\nsymplectic form.  Carried as a hypothesis so the theorem names its borrow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.IsSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.IsSelfDual","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SymSquareHolonomyIsRealType.lean#L72-L74","doc":"`V` is self-dual: isomorphic to its own dual. ","signatureChunk":0}]}